SOURCES={'collect.sh': '#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# MI300X evidence collector — Phase A (read-only system/stack inventory)\n# plus optional Phase B/C (capability probes / microbenchmarks) if a\n# torch-bearing python is found. SAFE BY DEFAULT: phase A never allocates\n# GPU memory, changes no settings, writes only into its own evidence dir.\n#\n# Usage:\n#   ./collect.sh                 # read-only inventory + capability probes\n#   ./collect.sh --bench         # + time-boxed microbenchmarks (one GPU)\n#   ./collect.sh --bench --gpu 3 # choose which GPU index benches use\n#\n# Env overrides: MI300X_PYTHON=/path/to/python (torch env), OUT_DIR=...\nset -u\nBENCH=0; GPU=0; EXTRA_PY="${MI300X_PYTHON:-}"\nwhile [ $# -gt 0 ]; do\n  case "$1" in\n    --bench) BENCH=1 ;;\n    --gpu) shift; GPU="${1:-0}" ;;\n    *) echo "unknown arg: $1" >&2; exit 2 ;;\n  esac\n  shift\ndone\n\nTS=$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S)\nHOST=$(hostname -s 2>/dev/null || echo host)\nBASE="${OUT_DIR:-mi300x-evidence-$HOST-$TS}"\nmkdir -p "$BASE/logs" "$BASE/probes"\necho "evidence dir: $BASE"\n\n# --- helper: run one command with timeout, always record something ---\nrun() { # run <name> <cmd...>\n  local name="$1"; shift\n  timeout 120 "$@" >"$BASE/logs/$name.txt" 2>&1 \\\n    || echo "__EXIT_$?__ (missing/stalled/timeout: $(printf \'%q \' "$@"))" >>"$BASE/logs/$name.txt"\n  echo "  [.] $name"\n}\n\necho "phase A: system/stack inventory (read-only)"\nrun date date -u\nrun uname uname -a\nrun os-release cat /etc/os-release\nrun lscpu lscpu\nrun numa numactl -H\nrun meminfo free -h\nrun dmidecode-sudoless dmidecode -t bios\nrun hwloc-info hwloc-info\nrun hwloc-topo hwloc-ls\nrun lspci lspci -nn\nrun kfd-devs ls -l /dev/kfd /dev/dri 2>/dev/null\nrun kfd-sys sh -c \'for f in /sys/class/kfd/kfd*/gpu_id /sys/class/kfd/kfd*/name /sys/class/kfd/kfd*/unique_id; do echo "== $f"; cat "$f" 2>/dev/null; done\'\n\necho "phase A: ROCm stack"\nrun rocm-smi-hw rocm-smi --showhw --json\nrun rocm-smi-product rocm-smi --showproductname --json\nrun rocm-smi-driver rocm-smi --showdriverversion --json\nrun rocm-smi-topo rocm-smi --showtopo\nrun rocm-smi-pids rocm-smi --showpids --json\nrun rocm-smi-mem rocm-smi --showmeminfo vram --json\nrun rocm-smi-power rocm-smi --showpower --json\nrun rocm-smi-clock rocm-smi --showclocks --json\nrun rocm-smi-temp rocm-smi --showtemp --json\nrun rocm-smi-busy rocm-smi --showbusy --json\nrun amd-smi-static amd-smi static\nrun amd-smi-metric amd-smi metric\nrun amd-smi-topo amd-smi topology\nrun rocminfo rocminfo\nrun hipconfig hipconfig --full\nrun hipcc hipcc --version\nrun rocm-vers cat /opt/rocm*/.info/version 2>/dev/null\nrun rocm-dirs ls -d /opt/rocm* /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/librccl* 2>/dev/null\nrun rocm-libs sh -c \'for d in /opt/rocm*/lib /opt/rocm*/lib64; do ls "$d"/libhipblaslt* "$d"/librccl* "$d"/librocwmma* "$d"/libMIOpen* "$d"/libamdhip* 2>/dev/null; done\'\nrun ldconfig-rocm sh -c \'ldconfig -p 2>/dev/null | grep -Ei "rccl|hipblas|hip\\.so|miopen|rocwmma|amdhip|composable"\'\nrun llvm-tools sh -c \'for d in /opt/rocm*/llvm/bin; do ls "$d"/llvm-objdump "$d"/llvm-mc "$d"/clang 2>/dev/null; done\'\nrun accel-sys ls /sys/class/accel 2>/dev/null\nrun driver-mod sh -c \'grep -H . /sys/module/amdgpu/version 2>/dev/null; lsmod | grep -E "amdgpu|amdkfd"\'\n\necho "phase A: python environments"\nPY_FOUND=""\nfor cand in "$EXTRA_PY" python3 python /opt/rocm*/bin/python3 $(ls /usr/bin/python3.* 2>/dev/null); do\n  [ -x "$cand" ] || continue\n  case "$cand" in *-config|*-config-*|[!/]*/python3.*-config) continue ;; esac\n  v=$("$cand" -c \'import torch,sys;print(torch.__version__, (getattr(torch.version,"hip",None) or "cuda"))\' 2>/dev/null || true)\n  # only accept output that looks like a torch version line (python3.x-config\n  # prints a usage banner and exits non-zero; without this check it is\n  # misread as a torch env - seen live on amd-mi300x 2026-11-14)\n  case "$v" in\n    [0-9]*.[0-9]*) echo "  [.] torch found: $cand -> $v"; PY_FOUND="$cand"; break ;;\n  esac\ndone\nif [ -n "$PY_FOUND" ]; then\n  "$PY_FOUND" -c \'import torch;print("torch",torch.__version__);print("hip",getattr(torch.version,"hip",None))\' >"$BASE/logs/torch-env.txt" 2>&1\n  "$PY_FOUND" -m pip list 2>/dev/null | grep -Ei \'torch|triton|numpy|nvidia|amd|rccl|transformers|safetensors\' >>"$BASE/logs/torch-env.txt" || true\n  "$PY_FOUND" -c \'import torch;print(torch.__config__.show())\' >>"$BASE/logs/torch-env.txt" 2>&1 || true\nelse\n  echo "  [!] no python with torch found — set MI300X_PYTHON=/path/to/python and rerun" | tee "$BASE/logs/torch-env.txt"\nfi\n\necho "phase A: environment variables (ROCm-relevant)"\nsh -c \'env | grep -Ei "ROCM|HIP|HSA|MIOPEN|NCCL|RCCL|GPU|TRITON" | sort\' >"$BASE/logs/env.txt" 2>&1 || echo "__none__" >"$BASE/logs/env.txt"\n\n# --- Phase B (capability probes, bounded single-GPU) and optional C ---\nif [ -n "$PY_FOUND" ]; then\n  SCRIPT_DIR=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)\n  ARGS="--gpu $GPU --out $BASE/probes"\n  [ "$BENCH" -eq 1 ] && ARGS="$ARGS --bench"\n  echo "phase B: capability probes (bounded, GPU $GPU)"\n  timeout 1500 "$PY_FOUND" "$SCRIPT_DIR/probes.py" cap $ARGS\n  rc=$?\n  echo "$rc" >"$BASE/probes/exit_code.txt"\n  if [ "$rc" -ne 0 ]; then echo "  [!] probes exited $rc — logs in $BASE/probes/probe_results.json"; fi\nelse\n  echo "phase B/C skipped: no torch python"\nfi\n\n# --- bundle ---\necho "bundling"\nSUMMARY="$BASE/SUMMARY.txt"\n{\n  echo "MI300X evidence bundle $HOST $TS"\n  echo "--- artifacts ---"; (cd "$BASE" && find . -type f | sort)\n  echo "--- key facts ---"\n  grep -m4 -E \'gfx|Marketing|Card series|GPU SKU\' "$BASE/logs/rocminfo.txt" "$BASE/logs/rocm-smi-product.txt" 2>/dev/null || true\n} >"$SUMMARY"\n(cd "$BASE" && find . -type f -exec sha256sum {} \\;) >"$BASE/SHA256SUMS.txt"\ntar czf "$BASE.tar.gz" "$BASE"\necho "DONE -> $BASE.tar.gz"\necho "send back the whole .tar.gz (it contains logs/, probes/, SHA256SUMS.txt)"\n', 'probes.py': '#!/usr/bin/env python\n"""MI300X capability probes for damendaemon #62 (MI300-class qual) and #719\n(CUDA+ROCm fleet split). Single-GPU, bounded, evidence-oriented:\n\n  cap sections: torch/ROCm env, device+arch props, dtype + FP8 variant\n  semantics (fn vs fnuz), torch._scaled_mm support matrix, a representative\n  Triton q4-dequant kernel (compile, correctness vs reference, .amdgcn ISA\n  dump), optional --bench: time-boxed D2D bandwidth + bf16/fp8 GEMM.\n\nWrites probe_results.json INCREMENTALLY so partial evidence survives a\ncrash or timeout. Allocates memory only on --gpu (default 0). Nothing here\nchanges system state. Run via collect.sh, or directly:\n  python probes.py cap --gpu 0 --out <dir> [--bench]\n"""\nimport argparse, json, os, shutil, sys, time\n\n\ndef _w(store, path):\n    tmp = path + \'.tmp\'\n    with open(tmp, \'w\') as f:\n        json.dump(store, f, indent=1, default=str)\n    os.replace(tmp, path)\n\n\ndef section(store, outpath, name, fn):\n    print(f\'[.] {name} ...\', flush=True)\n    t0 = time.time()\n    try:\n        res = fn()\n        if not isinstance(res, dict):\n            res = {\'value\': res}\n        res[\'_seconds\'] = round(time.time() - t0, 2)\n        print(f\'[+] {name} ok ({res["_seconds"]}s)\', flush=True)\n    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 - evidence, not control flow\n        res = {\'error\': f\'{type(e).__name__}: {e}\',\n               \'_seconds\': round(time.time() - t0, 2)}\n        print(f\'[!] {name} FAILED: {e}\', flush=True)\n    store[name] = res\n    _w(store, outpath)\n\n\ndef rocm_env():\n    keys = (\'ROCM_PATH\', \'HIP_PATH\', \'HSA_ENABLE_SDMA\', \'HSA_FORCE_FINE_GRAIN_PCIE\',\n            \'MIOPEN_FIND_MODE\', \'MIOPEN_USER_DB_PATH\', \'AMD_LOG_LEVEL\',\n            \'TRITON_CACHE_DIR\', \'HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES\', \'ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES\',\n            \'GPU_MAX_HW_QUEUES\', \'NCCL_\', \'RCCL_\', \'TORCH_BLAS_PREFER_\')\n    env = {k: os.environ[k] for k in os.environ if k.startswith(keys)}\n    return {\'captured\': env, \'count\': len(env)}\n\n\ndef device_props(gpu):\n    import torch\n    n = torch.cuda.device_count()\n    allp = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        try:\n            p = torch.cuda.get_device_properties(i)\n            allp.append({\'index\': i, \'name\': p.name,\n                         \'gcnArchName\': getattr(p, \'gcnArchName\', None),\n                         \'total_mem_GiB\': round(p.total_memory / 2**30, 1),\n                         \'sm_count\': p.multi_processor_count,\n                         \'is_integrated\': p.is_integrated,\n                         \'major\': p.major, \'minor\': p.minor})\n        except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n            allp.append({\'index\': i, \'error\': f\'{type(e).__name__}: {e}\'})\n    free, total = torch.cuda.mem_get_info(gpu)\n    return {\'count\': n, \'devices\': allp,\n            \'selected_gpu\': gpu,\n            \'free_GiB\': round(free / 2**30, 2),\n            \'total_GiB\': round(total / 2**30, 2)}\n\n\ndef dtype_scan(dev):\n    import torch\n    results = {}\n    names = [\'float16\', \'bfloat16\', \'float32\', \'float8_e4m3fn\', \'float8_e5m2\',\n             \'float8_e4m3fnuz\', \'float8_e5m2fnuz\', \'uint8\', \'int8\']\n    for name in names:\n        entry: dict = {\'exists\': hasattr(torch, name)}\n        if not entry[\'exists\']:\n            results[name] = entry\n            continue\n        dt = getattr(torch, name)\n        try:\n            entry[\'finfo_max\'] = (float(torch.finfo(dt).max)\n                                   if dt.is_floating_point else None)\n        except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n            entry[\'finfo_max\'] = f\'{type(e).__name__}: {e}\'\n        try:\n            a = torch.randn(64, device=dev).to(dt)\n            b = (a.to(torch.float32) * 2.0).to(dt)\n            _ = a.to(torch.float32) + b.to(torch.float32)\n            entry[\'cast_roundtrip_gpu\'] = \'ok\'\n        except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n            entry[\'cast_roundtrip_gpu\'] = f\'{type(e).__name__}: {e}\'\n        results[name] = entry\n    return results\n\n\nFP8 = (\'float8_e4m3fn\', \'float8_e4m3fnuz\', \'float8_e5m2\', \'float8_e5m2fnuz\')\n\n\ndef fp8_semantics(dev):\n    """Byte-level ground truth for FP8 variants. THE discriminator between\n    fn (CUDA-style, bias 7) and fnuz (AMD, bias 8): encoding of 1.0 is 0x38\n    vs 0x40 and finfo max 448 vs 240 (validated on CPU torch 2.13). Records\n    a small decode table straight from device memory so nothing is inferred\n    from headers."""\n    import torch\n    out = {}\n    for name in FP8:\n        if not hasattr(torch, name):\n            out[name] = {\'exists\': False}\n            continue\n        dt = getattr(torch, name)\n        info = {\'exists\': True}\n        try:\n            one = torch.tensor([1.0], dtype=torch.float32, device=dev).to(dt)\n            info[\'byte_of_1.0\'] = \'0x%02x\' % int(one.view(torch.uint8).item())\n            info[\'finfo_max\'] = float(torch.finfo(dt).max)\n            raw = torch.tensor(list(range(256)), dtype=torch.uint8, device=dev)\n            vals = raw.view(dt).float()\n            probe_bytes = [0x00, 0x38, 0x30, 0x7E, 0x7F, 0x80, 0xFF]\n            info[\'decode_table\'] = {\'0x%02x\' % b: float(vals[b].item())\n                                    for b in probe_bytes}\n            nanmask = torch.isnan(vals.cpu())\n            info[\'nan_bytes\'] = [\'0x%02x\' % i for i in\n                                 nanmask.nonzero().flatten().tolist()]\n        except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n            info[\'error\'] = f\'{type(e).__name__}: {e}\'\n        out[name] = info\n    return out\n\n\ndef scaled_mm_matrix(dev):\n    """Does this stack do FP8 matmul, with which input dtypes/layouts/scaling?\n    A plain bf16 matmul sanity anchor runs first; each fp8 x scaling cell\n    records max abs error vs fp32 on a 256x256x256 case or the exact error.\n    Scaling modes follow torch\'s TensorWise/RowWise contract exactly:\n      tensorwise: scale_a/scale_b both 1-element float tensors\n      rowwise:    scale_a (M,1), scale_b (1,N)   (column-major b required)\n    v1 of this probe mixed a per-row scale_a with a singleton scale_b and\n    every cell was rejected with \'Invalid scaling configuration\' on the\n    MI300X run (2026-11-14) - that was a probe defect, not a hardware\n    verdict; keep both modes explicit so the result is conclusive."""\n    import torch\n    out: dict = {\'has_scaled_mm\': hasattr(torch, \'_scaled_mm\')}\n    if not out[\'has_scaled_mm\']:\n        return out\n    M = K = N = 256\n    a32 = torch.randn(M, K, device=dev)\n    b32 = torch.randn(K, N, device=dev)\n    ref = a32 @ b32\n    bf = torch.matmul(a32.to(torch.bfloat16), b32.to(torch.bfloat16))\n    out[\'bf16_matmul_max_err\'] = (bf.float() - ref).abs().max().item()\n    modes = {\n        \'tw\': (torch.ones(1, device=dev), torch.ones(1, device=dev)),\n        \'rw\': (torch.ones(M, 1, device=dev), torch.ones(1, N, device=dev)),\n    }\n    for aname in FP8:\n        if not hasattr(torch, aname):\n            continue\n        for bname in FP8:\n            if not hasattr(torch, bname):\n                continue\n            for layout in (\'row\', \'col\'):\n                for mname, (sa, sb) in modes.items():\n                    key = (f\'{aname.split("_")[-1]}x{bname.split("_")[-1]}\'\n                           f\':{layout}:{mname}\')\n                    try:\n                        A = a32.to(getattr(torch, aname))\n                        B = b32.to(getattr(torch, bname))\n                        if layout == \'col\':\n                            B = B.t().contiguous().t()\n                        C = torch._scaled_mm(A, B, scale_a=sa, scale_b=sb,\n                                             out_dtype=torch.bfloat16)\n                        out[key] = {\'ok\': True,\n                                    \'max_abs_err_vs_fp32\': round(\n                                        (C.float() - ref).abs().max().item(), 4)}\n                    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n                        out[key] = {\'ok\': False,\n                                    \'err\': f\'{type(e).__name__}: {str(e)[:300]}\'}\n    return out\n\n\ndef triton_q4(dev, out_dir):\n    """Representative damendaemon kernel shape (q4_0-style: fp16 scale +\n    16 packed nibble bytes per 32 values) compiled through Triton on the\n    AMD backend. Verifies numerics vs a plain-torch reference, then copies\n    the compiled .amdgcn/.hsaco from the Triton cache into evidence."""\n    import torch\n    import triton\n    import triton.language as tl\n\n    @triton.jit\n    def _q4_dequant(S, P, Y, BLOCKS: tl.constexpr):\n        b = tl.program_id(0)\n        s = tl.load(S + b).to(tl.float32)\n        p = tl.load(P + b * 16 + tl.arange(0, 16))\n        lo = (p & 0x0F).to(tl.float32) - 8.0\n        hi = (p >> 4).to(tl.float32) - 8.0\n        base = b * 32\n        off = base + tl.arange(0, 16)\n        tl.store(Y + off, lo * s)\n        tl.store(Y + off + 16, hi * s)\n\n    res = {\'triton_version\': triton.__version__}\n    blocks = 4096\n    torch.manual_seed(0)\n    scales = (torch.randn(blocks).to(torch.float16) * 0.25).to(dev)\n    packed_cpu = torch.randint(0, 256, (blocks, 16), dtype=torch.uint8)\n    packed = packed_cpu.to(dev)\n    # plain-torch CPU reference, vectorized (same arithmetic the kernel does)\n    vals = torch.empty(blocks, 32, dtype=torch.float32)\n    vals[:, :16] = (packed_cpu & 0x0F).to(torch.float32) - 8.0\n    vals[:, 16:] = (packed_cpu >> 4).to(torch.float32) - 8.0\n    ref = (vals * scales.cpu().to(torch.float32).unsqueeze(1)).reshape(-1).to(dev)\n    y = torch.empty_like(ref)\n    _q4_dequant[(blocks,)](scales, packed, y, BLOCKS=blocks)\n    res[\'max_abs_err_vs_reference\'] = (y - ref).abs().max().item()\n    res[\'pass\'] = bool((y - ref).abs().max().item() < 1e-3)\n    # capture compiled artifacts from the triton cache\n    try:\n        cache = os.environ.get(\'TRITON_CACHE_DIR\',\n                               os.path.expanduser(\'~/.triton/cache\'))\n        hits = []\n        for root, _dirs, files in os.walk(cache):\n            age = time.time() - os.path.getmtime(root)\n            if age < 120:\n                for fn in files:\n                    if fn.endswith((\'.amdgcn\', \'.hsaco\', \'.ttir\', \'.ttgir\')):\n                        src = os.path.join(root, fn)\n                        dst = os.path.join(out_dir, \'triton_\' + fn)\n                        shutil.copy2(src, dst)\n                        hits.append({\'file\': fn, \'bytes\': os.path.getsize(src)})\n        res[\'isa_artifacts\'] = hits\n    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n        res[\'isa_capture_error\'] = f\'{type(e).__name__}: {e}\'\n    return res\n\n\ndef benches(dev, budget_s):\n    """Opt-in, time-boxed: HBM D2D bandwidth and one bf16 + one fp8 GEMM\n    size. No throughput claims beyond these numbers; sized to fit free VRAM."""\n    import torch\n    out = {\'budget_s\': budget_s}\n    deadline = time.monotonic() + budget_s\n    free, total = torch.cuda.mem_get_info(dev)\n    out[\'free_GiB_at_start\'] = round(free / 2**30, 2)\n    nbytes = min(2 * 2**30, int(free * 0.4))\n    src = torch.empty(nbytes, dtype=torch.uint8, device=dev)\n    dst = torch.empty_like(src)\n    for _ in range(2):\n        dst.copy_(src)\n    torch.cuda.synchronize()\n    t0 = time.perf_counter()\n    iters = 5\n    for _ in range(iters):\n        dst.copy_(src)\n    torch.cuda.synchronize()\n    dt = (time.perf_counter() - t0) / iters\n    out[\'d2d_copy_GBs_rw\'] = round(2 * nbytes / dt / 1e9, 1)\n    del src, dst\n    if time.monotonic() < deadline:\n        m = 8192\n        A = torch.randn(m, m, device=dev, dtype=torch.bfloat16)\n        B = torch.randn(m, m, device=dev, dtype=torch.bfloat16)\n        for _ in range(3):\n            A @ B\n        torch.cuda.synchronize()\n        t0 = time.perf_counter()\n        for _ in range(10):\n            A @ B\n        torch.cuda.synchronize()\n        dt = (time.perf_counter() - t0) / 10\n        out[\'bf16_gemm_8192_tflops\'] = round(2 * m**3 / dt / 1e12, 1)\n        del A, B\n    if time.monotonic() < deadline and hasattr(torch, \'_scaled_mm\'):\n        try:\n            m = 8192\n            A = torch.randn(m, m, device=dev).to(torch.float8_e4m3fnuz\n                                                 if hasattr(torch,\n                                                    \'float8_e4m3fnuz\')\n                                                 else torch.float8_e4m3fn)\n            B = torch.randn(m, m, device=dev).to(A.dtype).t().contiguous().t()\n            # tensorwise scaling first (v1\'s mixed rowwise-a/singleton-b was\n            # rejected on MI300X); rowwise as fallback\n            sa = torch.ones(1, device=dev)\n            sb = torch.ones(1, device=dev)\n            try:\n                for _ in range(3):\n                    torch._scaled_mm(A, B, scale_a=sa, scale_b=sb,\n                                     out_dtype=torch.bfloat16)\n                torch.cuda.synchronize()\n                out[\'fp8_gemm_scaling\'] = \'tensorwise\'\n            except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n                sa = torch.ones(m, 1, device=dev)\n                sb = torch.ones(1, m, device=dev)\n                for _ in range(3):\n                    torch._scaled_mm(A, B, scale_a=sa, scale_b=sb,\n                                     out_dtype=torch.bfloat16)\n                torch.cuda.synchronize()\n                out[\'fp8_gemm_scaling\'] = \'rowwise\'\n            t0 = time.perf_counter()\n            for _ in range(10):\n                torch._scaled_mm(A, B, scale_a=sa, scale_b=sb,\n                                 out_dtype=torch.bfloat16)\n            torch.cuda.synchronize()\n            dt = (time.perf_counter() - t0) / 10\n            out[\'fp8_gemm_8192_dtype\'] = str(A.dtype)\n            out[\'fp8_gemm_8192_tflops\'] = round(2 * m**3 / dt / 1e12, 1)\n        except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n            out[\'fp8_gemm_error\'] = f\'{type(e).__name__}: {str(e)[:200]}\'\n    torch.cuda.empty_cache()\n    out[\'free_GiB_at_end\'] = round(\n        torch.cuda.mem_get_info(dev)[0] / 2**30, 2)\n    return out\n\n\ndef main():\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=((__doc__ or \'\') .splitlines() or [\'MI300X probes\'])[0])\n    p.add_argument(\'mode\', choices=[\'cap\'],\n                   help=\'cap = capability probes (single GPU, bounded)\')\n    p.add_argument(\'--gpu\', type=int, default=0, help=\'GPU index to probe\')\n    p.add_argument(\'--out\', default=\'.\', help=\'output directory\')\n    p.add_argument(\'--bench\', action=\'store_true\',\n                   help=\'opt-in: time-boxed bandwidth/GEMM microbenches\')\n    p.add_argument(\'--bench-budget\', type=int, default=120,\n                   help=\'wall-clock seconds allowed for benches\')\n    args = p.parse_args()\n    import platform\n    os.makedirs(args.out, exist_ok=True)\n    outpath = os.path.join(args.out, \'probe_results.json\')\n    store = {\'meta\': {\n        \'started_utc\': time.strftime(\'%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\', time.gmtime()),\n        \'host\': platform.node(),\n        \'python\': sys.version.split()[0],\n        \'argv\': sys.argv[1:],\n    }}\n    _w(store, outpath)\n    import torch\n    if not torch.cuda.is_available():\n        store[\'meta\'][\'error\'] = (\'torch.cuda.is_available() is False - no AMD \'\n                                  \'GPU visible to this torch build (check \'\n                                  \'driver, /dev/kfd access, HSA/ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES)\')\n        _w(store, outpath)\n        print(\'NO CUDA/HIP DEVICE VISIBLE - wrote meta.error, exiting 3\',\n              flush=True)\n        return 3\n    torch.cuda.set_device(args.gpu)\n    dev = torch.device(\'cuda\', args.gpu)\n    section(store, outpath, \'rocm_env\', rocm_env)\n    section(store, outpath, \'device_props\', lambda: device_props(args.gpu))\n    section(store, outpath, \'dtype_scan\', lambda: dtype_scan(dev))\n    section(store, outpath, \'fp8_semantics\', lambda: fp8_semantics(dev))\n    section(store, outpath, \'scaled_mm_matrix\', lambda: scaled_mm_matrix(dev))\n    section(store, outpath, \'triton_q4\', lambda: triton_q4(dev, args.out))\n    if args.bench:\n        section(store, outpath, \'benches\',\n                lambda: benches(dev, args.bench_budget))\n    store[\'meta\'][\'finished_utc\'] = time.strftime(\n        \'%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\', time.gmtime())\n    _w(store, outpath)\n    print(f\'PROBES DONE -> {outpath}\', flush=True)\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \'__main__\':\n    sys.exit(main())\n', 'README.md': '# MI300X evidence collection (issues #62, #719)\n\nBounded, read-only probes for qualifying an MI300-class datacenter host\nindependently of HOMER (#62) and for the ROCm side of the CUDA+ROCm fleet\nsplit (#719). Nothing here changes system state; GPU memory is allocated\nonly on the single `--gpu` index, and only for capability checks and\nopt-in benches.\n\n## What to run\n\n```bash\nchmod +x collect.sh\n./collect.sh                # read-only inventory + capability probes\n./collect.sh --bench        # + time-boxed bandwidth/GEMM microbenches (~2 min)\n./collect.sh --bench --gpu 3   # pick which GPU the probes/benches use\n```\n\nIf the torch env isn\'t on the default `python3`, point at it:\n\n```bash\nMI300_PYTHON=/opt/conda/envs/rocm/bin/python ./collect.sh --bench\n```\n\nSend back the printed `.tar.gz`. If something stalls, individual logs are\nin the evidence dir — partial bundles still beat nothing (every phase\nwrites as it goes, `probes.py` rewrites `probe_results.json` after each\nsection).\n\n## What each phase collects and why\n\n| Phase | Evidence | Feeds |\n|---|---|---|\n| A logs | `rocminfo`, `rocm-smi`/`amd-smi` (hw, product, driver, topo, pids, mem, power, clocks), `hipconfig --full`, `lscpu`/`numactl -H` (NUMA), `lspci`, `/sys/class/kfd`, ldconfig ROCm libs (RCCL/hipBLASLt/MIOpen/hip), kernel module version | #62 "pin actual SKU, memory/NUMA/interconnect, ROCm/HIP stack"; fleet-fit arithmetic (VRAM + host RAM inventory) |\n| B probes | device props for ALL GPUs (`gcnArchName` — expect `gfx942`), dtype scan, **FP8 fn vs fnuz byte-level decode tables** (1.0 = 0x38 vs 0x40, max 448 vs 240), `torch._scaled_mm` dtype/layout support matrix with error strings, **Triton q4-dequant kernel**: compile + numeric check vs plain-torch reference + `.amdgcn`/`.hsaco` ISA dump | #62 "capability-based backend selection, primitive arithmetic, FP8/packed formats"; #719 GLM q4 kernels on ROCm; the CUDA→ROCm FP8-variant boundary |\n| C benches (opt-in) | HBM D2D copy GB/s (read+write), bf16 8192³ GEMM TFLOPs, fp8 scaled_mm TFLOPs — sized to free VRAM, hard wall-clock budget | #62 "no unmeasured extrapolation"; #54 scorecard cells |\n\nExpected-ish MI300X shapes (for sanity-checking the returned evidence, not\ngates): ~192 GiB HBM3 per GPU, >3 TB/s D2D, gfx942, RCCL for collectives.\nThe probes never assume these — they measure.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `rocm-smi` may be deprecated on your stack in favor of `amd-smi`; both\n  are captured, failures recorded per-command.\n- The Triton ISA capture copies recently-touched cache entries (`.amdgcn`,\n  `.hsaco`, `.ttir`) — if your `TRITON_CACHE_DIR` is elsewhere it\'s picked\n  up automatically.\n- Multi-GPU collectives (RCCL all-reduce, P2P over xGMI) are NOT probed\n  here — that needs a later two-rank cell under #51 once single-GPU\n  capability is established.\n'}
